<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chiang Rai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1262">1262</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chiang Rai is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a> on the Kok River, founded by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mangrai">Mangrai</a> of Ngoenyang in 1262. It served as Mangrai's base for his expansion southward, which led to the conquest of Hariphunchai in 1292 and the founding of Chiang Mai in 1296 as the capital of Lan Na. It remained an important town of Lan Na and is now a provincial capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chiang-rai.jpg" alt="Chiang Rai" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chainwit. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%AC%E0%B8%B4%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B2%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%8A%E0%B8%B5%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2_Chiang_Rai_Clock_Tower.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
